      "content": "Targeted welfare programs are fundamentally broken because they rely on outdated data and bureaucratic inefficiencies that waste billions on red tape rather than actual human need. While UBI does carry fiscal and inflation risks, these are manageable through progressive taxation and technological automation, whereas the current system's structural flaws cause far more harm by leaving vulnerable populations without adequate support. We must prioritize a UBI framework to ensure every citizen has the dignity and security to thrive, rather than continuing to prop up a broken system that fails the most vulnerable.",
      "source": "target",
